  "source_brief": {
    "silhouette": "A broad low center of gravity, square apron panels and a single large two-handed hammer held across the body. One uncovered upper sleeve breaks the armored outline without exposing a vulnerable-looking costume.",
    "face": "Deep brown skin, bright gray eyes and black hair in a thick high braid coiled at the back. A stern resting expression softens during the victory pose.",
    "costume": "Red workshop coat beneath segmented shoulder armor, a short split leather apron and heavy wrapped boots. Metal is limited to the shoulders, wrists and tool head.",
    "palette": "Brick red #A64E45; soot #4A4343; honey leather #A67E4B; steel #AAB2B7.",
    "equipment": "A blocky fantasy forge hammer with a large beveled face and short decorative rune strip. The tool reads from shape rather than detailed mechanical parts.",
    "signature": "Wide hammer bar, red split coat and squared apron silhouette.",
    "materials": "Coarse leather, wool, lightly worn iron and painted wood. Use broad edge accents to suggest craft rather than gritty damage.",
    "back": "A simple crossed harness stabilizes the hammer rest pose; the braid coil stays above the shoulder blades and outside the swing path.",
    "animation": "Idle holds the hammer diagonally with settled elbows. Walk uses strong grounded steps. Basics use a short overhead arc. The active pivots through one wide sweep, then returns to the same tile.",
    "vfx": "A low pale-gold sweep arc traces only the adjacent-cell ring; no knockback or extra stun.",
    "audio": "A broad whoosh and compact stone-on-metal fantasy impact, limited to one main active sound even with several victims.",
    "risk": "The sweep must not imply a larger hit radius than the data. Avoid excessive root rotation that changes gameplay facing or shifts the feet."
  },
